 "final_summary": "The bug was in tracker/query.py where priority_min filtering used `priority > ?` instead of `priority >= ?`, making it exclusive. This was fixed by changing the condition to `priority >= ?`, ensuring tasks with the minimum priority are included as required by the API contract.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/query.py b/tracker/query.py\nindex 40b062f..b7b7d50 100644\n--- a/tracker/query.py\n+++ b/tracker/query.py\n@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@ def build_filters(params, now_iso=None):\n         args.append(owner)\n     priority_min = parse_int(params.get(\"priority_min\"), name=\"priority_min\")\n     if priority_min is not None:\n-        clauses.append(\"priority > ?\")\n+        clauses.append(\"priority >= ?\")\n         args.append(priority_min)\n     text = params.get(\"q\")\n     if text and str(text).strip():\n",
